# flowdeck

> Human↔AI collaboration via `TODO.md` files.
> `## BOT` is Claude's inbox — tasks Claude should complete.
> `## HUMAN` is your inbox — things Claude needs from you.
> Run `flowdeck play -m "<what you did>"` to commit and hand off to Claude, or `flowdeck play` to hand off without a new commit.

## BOT
- [ ] Task for Claude to do
- [x] Completed task
  > short note on what was done

## HUMAN
- [ ] Question needing your input?
  > _answer:_
- [x] Answered question
  > _answer:_ your answer here

## ACTIONS
<!-- optional: a dormant menu of possible actions — move a line to ## BOT or ## HUMAN to activate it -->
- [ ] some-action — [describe the input it needs]

## STOCK
<!-- optional: standing tasks kept out of ## BOT until picked up -->
- [ ] recurring scan or check

#### COMMENTS
- Notable findings from execution: unexpected behaviour, real validations, non-obvious decisions. Added by Claude, not you.

## OUTCOME
<!-- written automatically by `play` once every ## BOT task is checked -->
What was built, key files or changes, and how to use the deliverable.

