---

Reference, not boilerplate — delete any section you're not using from your own cards.

- **`depends: <slug>`** (optional, right after the title) — declares this card waits on another. `turn` orders execution accordingly; `play` warns if the dependency still has open `## BOT` items (`--no-dep-check` skips the check).
- **YAML frontmatter** (`---`-fenced block above the `# title`) — all card metadata. Supported keys:
  - `lifecycle: one-shot | recurring | standing | ritual` — `recurring` keeps the card on the table (BOT checkboxes reset after play); `ritual` + `recurrence: on-demand` excludes the card from `turn` sweeps. Instrument cards (recurring/ritual) that don't belong on the table live in the `_sleeve/` pile — `flowdeck sleeve <card>` moves them there; they play in place, renew via `blank`, and are never melded. `flowdeck sleeve` refuses `one-shot` cards without `--force`.
  - `recurrence: on-demand | weekly | daily | …` — `on-demand` suppresses automatic `turn` inclusion; other values are logged after play resets checkboxes
  - `nick: Casual | Glinder | Shark | Wale` — recommended model alias; precedence: `--model` > `model:` > `nick:` > `agents.json` default
  - `model: Shark` — hard-pins the alias, overrides `nick:`
  - `review: true` — runs an automatic reviewer pass during `turn`
  - `skill: <id>` — bound skill identifier (ritual cards)
  - `projects: [a, b]` — cross-project scope (ritual cards)
  - `permissions: standard | read-only | unrestricted` — portable execution policy; unrestricted also requires this card's exact canonical path in project-local `permissions.unrestrictedCards`
- See `docs/card-metadata-spec.md` for the full schema and migration guide from comment markers.
- **`> _answer:_`** stub under a `## HUMAN` question — leave it blank until you answer it, or run `flowdeck kemps` to have Claude propose an answer as `> _kemps:_`.
- **`## ACTIONS`** / **`## STOCK`** — optional sections some decks use for dormant action menus and standing scan tasks; the CLI doesn't parse them specially, but Claude honors the convention when it sees them.

> Advanced: cards can bind tool output to `$var`s — see README "Tool Binding (advanced)".
